Final observations portable byte bundle

Portable original bytes of completed controlled160, analysis2/strict comparison, eight matched movies, a preserved FAILED outer-route movie and independent worst movie, plus one separate no-live-PNG technical control when present, original blocked queues and closure v2, original GUI failure and GUIv2, C3 delivery/52 with C4 test-only bridge, six controlled map pairs, completed bounded design/visual reviews, alpha calibration and restored forest PLAN ONLY. Outer route and Q6 remain failed; byte collection/compression does not grant engineering, content, fun, device or player PASS.

index.members.original_path is the original repository-relative restore path. stored is relative to this bundle. sha256 hashes ORIGINAL bytes; stored_sha256 hashes the actual stored file (including gzip). Quality records referencing a stored .gz MUST use stored_sha256, never the original JSON SHA.
Markdown source bytes use .md.source; restoration returns their exact .md names. AVI is explicitly excluded with measured SHA/size; each MP4, PNG and raw trace remains. The original outer attempt stays FAILED (7 assertions/1 failure, target=false, exit1). Derived failed media and independent closure v2 are collection records, not route or engineering PASS. An optional no-live-PNG observer has separate results and post-extracted video frames; it never replaces the original failure or establishes TTL causality. Already archived rejected Q6/old baseline trees are referenced, not recopied. C2/current identical action MP4s may share stored bytes with separate restorable paths.

Restore without engines: python3 restore.py --root /tmp/new-isolated-observation-root
Never overwrites differing files. --resume-identical permits only identical skips. A PACKAGING_FAILED.json without the final index is incomplete; retain it.

Consumer coverage inventory belongs separately, uncompressed, at docs/evidence/plains_redesign/acceptance/consumer_inventory.json; this packager does not create or alter that acceptance record.
Embedded historical absolute paths inside original JSON remain unchanged by design; restore verifies original bytes at repository-relative paths, not a promise that every archived analyzer can replay without an explicit relocation adapter.
